[{"title":"SMCForecast","page":"SMCForecast","location":"#SMCForecast","category":"section","text":""},{"title":"Installation","page":"SMCForecast","location":"#Installation","category":"section","text":"SMCForecast can be installed using the Julia package manager. From the Julia REPL, type ] to enter the Pkg REPL mode and run\n\npkg> add SMCForecast"},{"title":"API","page":"SMCForecast","location":"#API","category":"section","text":""},{"title":"SMCForecast.IdentityAdjustment","page":"SMCForecast","location":"#SMCForecast.IdentityAdjustment","category":"type","text":"No exogenous adjustment: the latent level is used as-is.\n\n\n\n\n\n"},{"title":"SMCForecast.LinearAdjustment","page":"SMCForecast","location":"#SMCForecast.LinearAdjustment","category":"type","text":"Multiplicative adjustment: prod_i (coefficients[i] + 1) over active (> 0) regressors.\n\n\n\n\n\n"},{"title":"SMCForecast.LocalLevel","page":"SMCForecast","location":"#SMCForecast.LocalLevel","category":"type","text":"Local level model\n\n\n\n\n\n"},{"title":"SMCForecast.LocalLevelCountStockoutModel","page":"SMCForecast","location":"#SMCForecast.LocalLevelCountStockoutModel","category":"type","text":"LocalLevelCountStockoutModel{A<:MeanAdjustment}\n\nA local-level, zero-inflated generalized-Poisson count model with a hidden 2-state (in-stock/stockout) Markov chain, parameterized by a MeanAdjustment that describes how the latent level is adjusted for exogenous effects.\n\nLocalLevelCountStockout, LocalLevelCountStockoutExplanatory, and LocalLevelCountStockoutExplanatoryML are aliases of this type with IdentityAdjustment, LinearAdjustment, and TreeAdjustment respectively; use their keyword constructors rather than constructing this type directly.\n\ninitial_state_weights and adjust_initial_value preserve two pre-existing differences between those three variants' initial-state sampling (the Explanatory variant historically did not re-derive its initial-state weights from level_matrix, and did not apply the exogenous adjustment to its initial value): they are not modeled as arbitrary knobs, just as the minimal surface needed to keep each variant's existing behavior identical after sharing this implementation.\n\n\n\n\n\n"},{"title":"SMCForecast.SMC","page":"SMCForecast","location":"#SMCForecast.SMC","category":"type","text":"Particle filter\n\n\n\n\n\n"},{"title":"SMCForecast.TreeAdjustment","page":"SMCForecast","location":"#SMCForecast.TreeAdjustment","category":"type","text":"Adjustment given by a (possibly leaf-value-overridden) regression tree over the regressors.\n\n\n\n\n\n"},{"title":"SMCForecast.filter!","page":"SMCForecast","location":"#SMCForecast.filter!-Union{Tuple{U}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{SMC{T, U}, Vector{Float64}}} where {T<:(StaticArraysCore.SizedVector{S, T} where {S, T}), U<:SMCForecast.SMCSystem{T}}","category":"method","text":"filter!(smc::SMC{T, U}, observations::Array{Float64, 1}; record=true) where {T <: SizedVector, U <: SMCSystem{T}}\n\nCompute the filtered distribution.\n\n\n\n\n\n"},{"title":"SMCForecast.filter!","page":"SMCForecast","location":"#SMCForecast.filter!-Union{Tuple{U}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{SMC{T, U}, Vector{Union{Missing, Float64}}}} where {T<:(StaticArraysCore.SizedVector{S, T} where {S, T}), U<:SMCForecast.SMCSystem{T}}","category":"method","text":"filter!(smc::SMC{T, U}, observations::Array{Union{Float64, Missing}, 1}; record=true) where {T <: SizedVector, U <: SMCSystem{T}}\n\nCompute the filtered distribution.\n\n\n\n\n\n"},{"title":"SMCForecast.initialize!","page":"SMCForecast","location":"#SMCForecast.initialize!-Union{Tuple{SMC{T, U}}, Tuple{U}, Tuple{T}} where {T<:(StaticArraysCore.SizedVector{S, T} where {S, T}), U<:SMCForecast.SMCSystem{T}}","category":"method","text":"initialize!(smc::SMC{T, U}) where {T <: SizedVector, U <: SMCSystem{T}}\n\nInitializes the particle filter.\n\n\n\n\n\n"}]
